================================================================================
Patterns (ideas, not code)
================================================================================

Design *patterns* — never source — were informed by public prior art: a
Claude-Code-style permission ladder, aider-style token-budgeted repo maps,
event-core/runtime-model-discovery patterns common to OSS coding agents, and the
Karpathy "LLM-Wiki" concept. No code was copied from any of these; the naming and
mode vocabulary that overlap with other tools are non-protectable conventions.

================================================================================
Third-party runtime dependencies
================================================================================

At runtime this software depends only on ordinary open-source libraries (React,
Ink, Zod, undici, string-width, smol-toml, yaml, and their transitive dependencies), each under its own
license. It ships no competitor runtime or binary.
